// Eyes and mouth are strokes, not fills -- a few short paths per mood
// instead of four separate illustrations. The mouths hang off the nose as
// a cat's "ω".
//
// `thriving` through `sleepy` read as waiting rather than suffering, which
// is the difference between "we got busy" and "you failed it".
//
// `withdrawn` frowns, at the user's explicit direction (carried over from
// the dog). Worth knowing if you're about to change it back or forward: the
// pet was chosen over a streak counter precisely because a streak resetting
// assigns blame, and a downturned mouth is the same message with a face on
// it -- shown on the days someone was busiest. Decide it deliberately
// either way rather than inheriting it.
